      "statement": "Every nonempty strictly positive sample has a unique MLE for the free scale. If any observation is zero, the likelihood is zero for every scale, so every scale ties and there is no unique estimate. Such samples are rejected. With the scale held, only the likelihood is evaluated, and zero observations are still rejected.",
